  "query_preview": "..\n(Tuesday through Sunday)\nIssued at 1204 AM CDT Mon Sep 14 2026\n\nHot and dry weather will persist across the area for the upcoming \nweek, as upper level high pressure continues to influence the \nregion. The upper level ridge will be situated across the southeast \nUS through much of the weak, with  West Central Texas on the western \nperiphery of the upper ridge. Highs this week will be in the upper \n90s to around 100 degrees each afternoon, with overnight lows mainly \nin the 70s. \n\nModels show an upper level trough moving across the Rockies and into \nthe Plains by next weekend, with a possible cold front moving into \nthe area by the end of next weekend. Latest guidance is still \nshowing the potential for some showers and thunderstorms by this \ntime, along with cooler temperatures, with highs cooling into the \nlower 90s by next Sunday, The forecast will remain dry through \nFriday, with a low chance (20-40%) for precipitation by next \nweekend.",
